darwin: Shift in menu key equivalents as AppKit has it

An accelerator with Shift and a character key, as "CmdOrCtrl+Shift+J",
became the NSMenuItem key equivalent "j" with Shift in the modifier mask.
AppKit shows that as ⇧⌘J, but matches it with the key without Shift too:
on macOS 26 Cmd+J ran the item of Cmd+Shift+J when that item came first
in the menu bar, and Cmd+Shift+J as typed (charactersIgnoringModifiers
"J") matched no item.

AppKit's own menus give the character Shift types and leave Shift out of
the mask: "J" for Shift+J, and for keys that are not letters the
character a US keyboard types with Shift ("!" for 1, "?" for /). The key
equivalent is now made so; keys Shift types nothing else with (Enter,
the arrows, F1–F12) keep Shift in the mask. Menu bar items and context
menus share the conversion.

Test: TestKeyEquivalentShift (internal/darwin).

diff --git a/internal/darwin/menu.go b/internal/darwin/menu.go
